2) Diffusion Domain Expansion (2605.23275) -- closest direct competitor-in-spirit to Longform. Trains a small ViT 'coordinator' (RoPE, train-short/generalize-long) that reconciles overlapping patches' PREDICTED-CLEAN (z0_hat) outputs instead of naive overlap-averaging -- beats MultiDiffusion-style averaging by a wide margin on FAD in its own (much weaker, raw-waveform UNet1d) setting. Maps cleanly onto z0_hat we already compute for FusionCC. Doesn't prove Longform's training-free SDEdit+crossfade is worse, but is a real quality-vs-simplicity argument worth a line in the frontier notes -- possible future ablation: small trained coordinator on SA3 z0_hat patches vs current crossfade.

3) Live Music Diffusion Models (2605.22717) -- UCSD/MIT/Adobe, passes both hard filters cleanly. Two pieces: a routing+attention-mask trick that makes block-outpainting diffusion KV-cacheable (candidate blueprint for streaming/low-latency SA3 continuation, untested against our differential attention); and ARC-Forcing, an RL-free adversarial rollout-level training objective that fixes gradual quality drift over long (2min) rollouts -- a genuinely different mechanism from FusionCC's single-block consistency loss. Speculative future tool if Longform long-track degradation is ever observed (none reported yet).

4) DEMON (2605.28657) -- not a control method, a streaming-systems paper (ACE-Step -> live-playable instrument, 12+ gen/sec, real musicians performed with it live). Same rectified-flow family + same Oobleck-VAE lineage as SAME. The framewise SDE source-blending step is basically a live, per-frame, continuously-adjustable generalization of Longform's whole-segment SDEdit re-anchor. Pure delivery-vehicle reference for 'if we ever build a real-time SA3 instrument,' not actionable now.

5) SegTune (2606.02638) -- song generation (vocals+lyrics, out of SA3's scope), but the hierarchical global+segment text-conditioning pattern (per-time-window natural-language captions, channel-concatenated not summed with the global style embedding) is a third control-design pattern alongside LatCH's trained probes and FusionCC's frozen-meter consistency. Also a clean reusable finding: concat beats linear-mix for fusing global+local conditioning in their ablations.

