Qiu et al. 2510.04212 — VERIFIED real+accurate (Qiu & Yao, ICLR 2026, code on GitHub; WebFetch'd the abstract). Mechanism as the report says: low-rank collapse in attention + compounding BIASED rounding errors → vicious cycle → catastrophic LOSS EXPLOSION; fix = a minimal flash-attn modification killing the rounding bias. My assessment on the three parts: >>> (1) THE DECISIVE EVIDENCE is empirical, not source: the Qiu failure mode IS catastrophic loss explosion — an acute, observable event. You say we don't see loss divergence → we are NOT in the acute Qiu regime. That's stronger than any kernel read, and it's the paper's own validation signature (the failure appears/vanishes with the fix). >>> (2) IMPORTANT NUANCE that corrects the easy answer (mine + W's earlier 'CK accumulates in fp32 → safe'): Qiu's whole contribution is that this failure SURVIVES fp32 accumulation — it's NOT the naive fp16-softmax-stats bug; it's a low-rank-collapse × input-rounding FEEDBACK loop. So 'our kernel fp32-accumulates' is NOT a full exoneration against Qiu specifically. The real exoneration is the no-explosion observation, full stop. >>> (3) KERNEL: SA3's DiT calls flash_attn_func (CK 2.8.4); eager fallback adp.py already fp32-softmaxes. CK 2.8.4 is a COMPILED HIP kernel — not source-auditable from the .venv (only the Python API + tests are there), and 2.8.4 predates the paper (Oct'25) so it almost certainly does NOT carry the paper's SPECIFIC minimal-mod mitigation. Net: probably-unmitigated-but-not-triggering. >>> CHEAP POSITIVE CHECK for your log-signature ask: the acute signature is attention LOW-RANK COLLAPSE + spectral-norm growth. A trained-checkpoint test: measure attention-map effective rank / row-cosine-similarity on a batch — if attention isn't collapsed to low-rank, Qiu's cycle isn't active (your loss-stability already says the acute mode is absent; this is the confirmatory positive). >>> RELATION TO OUR MELODY QUESTION — keep them SEPARATE: Qiu is a DISTINCT acute/explosion mode; it does NOT study sub-clinical degradation, so it's neither evidence for nor against our sub-dominant-melody-drowning hypothesis (which is a no-explosion effect). The fp32-residual/differential harness tests melody regardless of Qiu; don't let 'no Qiu explosion' get mis-read as 'precision is fine for melody' — different questions. >>> #68 fp16 DECISION: fp16 has MORE mantissa than bf16 (10 vs 7) → LESS of Qiu's rounding bias, so re Qiu specifically fp16-attn is plausibly SAFER than your current bf16; BUT fp16's narrower exponent range (5 vs 8 bits) is a separate overflow risk in the attention scores. So: canary run + watch for (a) loss instability, (b) attention spectral-norm growth; the paper's GitHub mitigation is a drop-in safety net if the signature appears. I'll add the 2510.04212 row to knowledge.md (abstract-verified, deep-read pending). Want me to write the effective-rank attention probe? It's ~20 lines on an existing checkpoint.

